# Legal documents — sync, acceptance bump, lawyer review versions

## 1. Sync App ↔ Web (same change)

When editing published legal content, review **all** related surfaces in the same task:

| Document | Canonical / locations |
|----------|------------------------|
| Privacy | Web `privacy.html` + EN in `js/locales/en-GB.js` (app links to web) |
| Terms (web) | `terms.html` + EN i18n |
| Cookies | `cookies.html` + EN i18n |
| Terms (app) | `TourAI.App/Resources/Terms/Terms.es-ES.html` + `Terms.en-GB.html` |
| Flows | `delete-account.html`, `reset-password.html` if wording changes |

Do not leave App Terms and Web Privacy/Terms out of sync for the same policy change.

## 2. Acceptance version (mandatory)

Follow **`legal-acceptance-version.mdc`**: bump `PublicConfig/Legal.CurrentVersion` and all fallbacks to **today’s** `YYYY-MM-DD`.

## 3. Lawyer review packages (delta-only folders)

Lawyer tooling lives **outside Git**:

`D:\Proyectos\Documents\legal-export`

**Never rewrite** a folder the lawyer already reviewed. For each new legal change set, create:

```
legal-export/reviews/yyyyMMdd - ShortTitle/
  SCOPE.md              # what changed vs last reviewed package (bullet list)
  DIFF-NOTES.md         # lawyer-facing delta only (new/changed clauses)
  outgoing/             # PDFs/ZIP of changed docs (or full package + SCOPE)
  lawyer-response/      # inbound answers/PDFs from the lawyer
```

Rules:

- Folder name starts with **`yyyyMMdd`** (session date) + short English or Spanish title.
- Put **only what is new or modified** in `DIFF-NOTES.md` / `outgoing/` so the lawyer does not re-read the whole corpus.
- Keep prior `reviews/*` folders immutable (archive, do not merge into them).
- Legacy flat files under `Revisiones hechas por Abogados\` stay as historical archive; **new** cycles use `reviews/`.

After content edits: regenerate PDFs with `legal-export/scripts/build-lawyer-package.js`, then copy the relevant outputs into that day’s `outgoing/`.

## 4. Reply to the owner

State: acceptance version bumped (or not), App/Web sync done, and the new `reviews/yyyyMMdd - …` folder path (or that lawyer package still needs generating).
